type\nescalate_only\naudience\nL1 Support Agent (authorized admin)\nrequired_role\nCoreID: Password Reset Admin\norg\nSolandra Corp\napplication\nCoreID Admin Console (mock)\nPurpose\nWhen a user's self-service password reset fails or the user has no working verification channel, the ticket escalates to L1. An authorized L1 agent with the Password Reset Admin role in CoreID resets the password directly from the admin console.\nBecause the agent's own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and role-gated, this flow does not send a one-time verification code to the user. That code-based check exists to authenticate an otherwise-unverified self-service claimant; an admin acting under an authenticated, role-scoped session establishes identity through the caller checklist instead (Step 3).\nProcedure\nInputs\nOpen ticket with the requester's employee ID and manager name on file\nYour own authenticated CoreID session with the Password Reset Admin role assigned\nCaller identity verification checklist (minimum 2 of 4 items matched)\nSteps\nStep 1: Ticket reviewed\nNavigation: Ticketing system → open ticket → Requester Details panel\nConfirm the ticket category reads Password Reset — Escalated, and note the requester's employee ID and manager name. ⚠️ Do not proceed if the ticket is missing a manager name — request it from the requester first.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 1 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.90 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a ticketing system, with the title \"Ticket #SOL-84213\" at the top. The purpose of the image is to display information about a specific ticket.\n\n* A ticketing system screenshot:\n\t+ The background is light gray.\n\t+ There are several sections on the left side of the image, including \"CoreID\", \"Admin Console\", \"Dashboard\", \"Tickets\", \"Users\", \"Reports\", and \"Settings\".\n\t+ The main content area is on the right side of the image, with a white background.\n* A list of categories 