nd it must not be disabled.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 4 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.90 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a password reset page for an employee named J. Employee, with a temporary password provided and a button to generate a new one.\n\n* The page is titled \"Reset Password - J. Employee\" and has a white background with black text.\n\t+ The title is centered at the top of the page.\n\t+ Below the title, there is a section with the temporary password and a checkbox to force a change at the next sign-in.\n\t+ There is a blue button labeled \"Generate Temporary Password\" below the checkbox.\n* The page has a navigation menu on the left side with the following options:\n\t+ CoreID\n\t+ Admin Console\n\t+ Dashboard\n\t+ Tickets\n\t+ Users\n\t+ Reports\n\t+ Settings\n* The page also has a header with the user's name and a link to sign out.\n\nThe page appears to be a standard password reset page, with a clear and concise layout. The temporary password is provided, and the user can choose to force a change at the next sign-in. The navigation menu provides access to other features and settings. Overall, the page is well-designed and easy to use. \n\nThere are no errors or warnings visible on the page. The page is likely used for employees to reset their passwords, and the temporary password is provided for security purposes. The page is well-designed and easy to use, making it a good user experience. \n\nThe likely issue category is Software/Application, with a severity of Medium. The reason is that the page is a standard password reset page, but it may not be suitable for all users or situations. The page is well-designed, but it may not be accessible to all users with disabilities. The page is also not secure, as the temporary password is visible and can be easily accessed by others. \n\nThe observed facts are:\n\n* The page is titled \"Reset Password - J. Employee\".\n* The page has a white background with blac