de the way self-service does?\nThe self-service code exists to authenticate an anonymous claimant with no other proof of identity. Here, identity is established two ways at once: your own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Confirm the ticket category and extract the requester's employee ID and manager name.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes a ticket review step, and the 'search_user' function in the Solandra platform matches this action. The 'employee_id' is required as input, and the response_schema provides the manager_name and status. This step is diagnostic and non-destructive, aligning with Stage 2 sequencing.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"search_user\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{entities.employee_id}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Confirm the user account is locked before proceeding.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP specifies confirming the account status as 'Locked'. The 'search_user' function's response_schema includes a 'status' field, which is used here for verification. This step ensures no password reset is performed on an unlocked account.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"search_user\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{entities.employee_id}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.is_locked == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 3,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Verify the caller's identity using at least 2 of 4 identity items (employee ID, manager name, department, last 4 digits of phone).\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes an identity verification step, and the 'verify_caller_identity' function in the Solandra platform matches this action. The required_inputs (employee_id, manager_name, department, phone_last4) are either provided as entities or inferred from prior steps. The response_schema confirms if verification passed.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"verify_caller_identity\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"user_id\": \"{{variables.employee_id}}\",\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{entities.employee_id}}\",\n      \"manager_name\": \"{{entities.manager_name}}\",\n      \"department\": \"{{entities.department}}\",\n      \"phone_last4\": \"{{entities.phone_last4}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.is_locked == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 90\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 4,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Generate a temporary password for the locked user and enable force change at next sign-in.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP describes generating a temporary password, and the 'generate_temporary_password' function in the Solandra platform matches this action. The required_input 'user_id' is derived from prior steps. The response_schema provides the temporary_password and confirms force_change_at_next_sign_in.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"generate_temporary_password\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"user_id\": \"{{variables.employee_id}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.verified == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 5,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Log the resolution audit note and set the ticket to Resolved.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The raw SOP specifies logging a resolution note and resolving the ticket. The 'resolve_ticket' function in the Solandra platform matches this action. The required_inputs (ticket_id, resolution_note) are provided as entities or inferred from prior steps. The response_schema confirms the ticket status.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"resolve_ticket\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"ticket_id\": \"{{entities.ticket_id}}\",\n      \"resolution_note\": \"Identity verified (2 of 4 checks). Temporary password issued via CoreID. Force-change-at-next-sign-in enabled. No OTP sent - admin-mediated reset per policy.\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.force_change_enabled == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is 